## 7. Add tasks, appointments, missing documents, and overdue work to the employee dashboard

### Current foundation

- The dashboard already returns tasks due today and overdue task counts/items.
- Upcoming appointments and appointments-today counts are available.
- Pending document counts and document action items are available.
- Cases without a next action or pending task are surfaced.
- Consultant queries are agency- and assignment-scoped.
- Dashboard calculations use the agency timezone.
- The frontend separates overdue work from today's/queued work.
- Dashboard rows open the related case or client.
- A separate `My Workload` page shows assigned cases, pending/overdue tasks, and documents under review.

### Remaining backend implementation

#### 7.1 Define exact work-queue semantics

Document and enforce what belongs to an employee dashboard:

- Tasks explicitly assigned to the employee.
- Unassigned tasks only when the employee owns/has primary responsibility for the case.
- Appointments assigned to the employee, plus clearly identified unassigned appointments on their cases if required.
- Documents requiring that employee's review, or unassigned review work for a case they own.
- Cases assigned to the employee that have no valid next action.

Do not show every appointment or document from an accessible case unless that is the intentional responsibility model.

#### 7.2 Separate missing documents from documents awaiting staff action

`Pending Documents` currently combines several statuses. Production queues should distinguish:

- `Missing from client`: requested and no usable upload received
- `Changes requested`: replacement required from client
- `Waiting for staff review`: uploaded or under review
- `Approved/finalized`: not an open work item

Return separate counts and arrays:

```text
missingDocuments
changesRequestedDocuments
documentsAwaitingReview
```

Include the request age and any requested due date. If document requests do not currently have a due date, add one where the agency needs deadline management.

#### 7.3 Return server-classified work items

Return a normalized queue model with:

```text
id
type
timingState
priority
title
dueAt
case
client
assignedTo
targetUrl
```

Using a single normalized work-item contract will keep dashboard, workload, notifications, and mobile views consistent.

#### 7.4 Add full queue endpoints

The dashboard summary currently limits most item lists to five records. Keep the summary lightweight, but add a paginated endpoint for the complete queue:

```text
GET /api/dashboard/work?type=&timingState=&page=&limit=
```

The `View all work` action should open this queue instead of depending on truncated dashboard arrays.

#### 7.5 Improve exact navigation targets

Return deep links from the backend or enough entity information to construct them consistently:

```text
/app/cases/:caseId?tab=tasks&taskId=:taskId
/app/cases/:caseId?tab=appointments&appointmentId=:appointmentId
/app/cases/:caseId?tab=documents&documentId=:documentId
```

Opening a dashboard item must select and highlight the exact record, not only open the top of the case profile.

#### 7.6 Add performance and reliability controls

- Add composite indexes for assigned pending tasks and upcoming appointments.
- Add an index for open document work by agency, status, case, and update/request time.
- Keep all queue queries agency-scoped.
- Confirm dashboard response time using production-scale data.
- Return an `asOf` timestamp and agency timezone.
- Avoid silently returning partial data if one queue query fails; log and expose a safe retryable error.

### Remaining frontend implementation

- Present separate sections for `Overdue`, `Due today`, `Upcoming appointments`, `Missing from client`, `Changes requested`, and `Waiting for review`.
- Do not mix missing-client work with staff-review work under one ambiguous document label.
- Show due time, overdue duration, priority, client, case type, and assignee.
- Make each card/row open the exact entity through a deep link.
- Preserve selected filters when returning from a case.
- Add empty, loading, error, and retry states per dashboard section.
- Add `View all` actions backed by paginated queue endpoints.
- Use the agency timezone provided by the API.
- Keep Front Desk on the lead workspace; do not expose the immigration case dashboard to that role.

### Acceptance tests

1. A consultant sees only assigned work and permitted unassigned case work.
2. An admin sees agency-wide work without cross-agency records.
3. Tasks appear in the correct overdue/due-today bucket for the agency timezone.
4. Cancelled and completed tasks do not appear in open queues.
5. An appointment appears for the correct employee and date.
6. A requested document without an upload appears as missing from the client.
7. An uploaded document appears as waiting for staff review, not missing.
8. A changes-requested document appears in the client-response queue.
9. Every dashboard item opens and highlights the exact task, appointment, or document.
10. More than five items can be reached through the full paginated work queue.
11. Dashboard queries remain responsive with production-sized agency data.

