## Cross-cutting implementation order

1. Finalize canonical applicant/profile ownership and add archival fields.
2. Add applicant duplicate detection, primary-applicant enforcement, and restore operations.
3. Create the shared server-side work/timing classification.
4. Add task cancellation metadata and preserve superseded workflow history.
5. Define and implement the canonical case timeline event contract.
6. Connect all case-domain services to the timeline contract.
7. Normalize dashboard work items and split document queues by responsibility.
8. Add paginated work-queue and cursor-based timeline endpoints.
9. Add exact frontend deep links, filters, archive/restore controls, and conflict handling.
10. Run authorization, timezone, concurrency, RLS, lifecycle, and production-volume tests.

## Definition of done for Priority 2

Priority 2 is complete when:

- Applicant information has one source of truth, duplicate protection, one primary applicant, safe archive/restore behavior, and immutable history.
- Task status and timing mean the same thing on every screen, cancellation preserves reason/actor/time, and workflow replacement cannot destroy history.
- The case timeline combines all important case events through one immutable, scoped, consistently ordered contract.
- Each employee dashboard shows precisely assigned daily work, separates overdue and document responsibility states, and opens the exact affected record.
- All four areas pass tenant isolation, role authorization, timezone, concurrency, archive/restore, and end-to-end case lifecycle tests.
